Build and serve a site, rebuilding when declared inputs change

Usage: diplodocus serve [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --color <COLOR>   Control terminal colors in help, diagnostics, and status output [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
      --config <PATH>   Path to the workspace configuration file [default: ./diplodocus.yaml]
      --no-progress     Print stage summaries instead of animated progress bars
      --output <PATH>   Directory in which to write the generated site [default: ./site]
      --host <ADDRESS>  Address on which to serve the generated site [default: 127.0.0.1]
  -q, --quiet           Suppress routine status output while retaining warnings and errors
      --port <PORT>     Port on which to serve the generated site [default: 8000]
      --live-reload     Refresh open browser pages after successful rebuilds
      --open            Open the local preview in a browser after the first successful build
  -h, --help            Print help
